    "text": "To determine how many dozen eggs Milo should buy, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the number of eggs needed:**\n   The recipe calls for 6 pounds of eggs. Each egg weighs \\(\\frac{1}{16}\\) of a pound. Therefore, the number of eggs required is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of eggs} = \\frac{6 \\text{ pounds}}{\\frac{1}{16} \\text{ pounds per egg}} = 6 \\times 16 = 96 \\text{ eggs}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Convert the number of eggs to dozens:**\n   Since there are 12 eggs in a dozen, we need to convert 96 eggs to dozens:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of dozens} = \\frac{96 \\text{ eggs}}{12 \\text{ eggs per dozen}} = 8 \\text{ dozens}\n   \\]\n\nThus, Milo should buy \\(\\boxed{8}\\) dozen eggs.",
